// Heading shape for a decision record, per docs/decisions/template.md.
//
// The hook entry that names this file (`md-adr` in .pre-commit-config.yaml)
// owns which documents it applies to; this file owns only the shape. It is an
// overlay, not a replacement: every other rule still comes from the project
// .markdownlint-cli2.jsonc, which markdownlint merges over this base. So MD043
// is the only rule here, and MD043 appears in no other config in the tree.
//
// The leading `*` matches the varying `# ADR-NNNN: <title>` line — one heading
// of any level and any text — which is also what lets one shape cover both a
// record and the template it was copied from. The array is a complete ordered
// list: a missing section, an extra section, a reordering, and a second
// `## Status` each fail, and the failure names the heading it did not expect.
//
// The file name must end in a configuration name markdownlint recognises, so
// `adr.markdownlint-cli2.jsonc` is loadable and `adr.jsonc` is not.
{
  "config": {
    "MD043": {
      "headings": [
        "*",
        "## Context and Problem Statement",
        "## Considered Options",
        "## Decision Outcome",
        "## Consequences",
        "## Status"
      ]
    }
  }
}
